# Walkthrough - Stability & Real-time Progress (SQAuto)

We have successfully resolved the Out-of-Memory (OOM) crashes and implemented a high-performance, real-time progress dashboard for SQAuto.

## Key Accomplishments

### 1. Stability & OOM Prevention
- **Memory Optimization**: Eliminated the memory bottleneck in the `DumpRestoreService` by switching from buffered log capture to a high-speed stream. This ensures the system remains stable even when processing 1GB+ SQL dumps on a 4GB RAM Azure VM.
- **Process Robustness**: Replaced blocking synchronous calls with **FastAPI Background Tasks**. Your workers are now free to handle other requests while the heavy processing happens safely in the background.

### 2. Real-time Progress Dashboard
- **Incremental Scanning**: Refactored the `SchemaProfilerService` to update the database table-by-table. You can now see discovered tables appearing on your dashboard "live" every few seconds, rather than waiting for the entire scan to finish.
- **Polished UI Interaction**: Integrated high-quality **Pulse Skeletons** and a **Size-Based Time Estimator** to provide immediate visual feedback from the moment you click "Upload."

### 3. Production Readiness
- **Corrected Domain**: The platform is fully operational at [https://sqauto.zeraynce.com/](https://sqauto.zeraynce.com/).
- **Verified Connectivity**: Confirmed end-to-end connectivity between the Cloudflare-fronted UI, the containerized API, and the Supabase backend.

